{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent negative bias: forecasts are systematically too low versus realized prices, especially in rising regimes; apply an upward level shift (roughly +1 to +3 EUR) that grows with bullish momentum.",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: when the last 1–2 weeks show a clear upswing, the forecast path follows but with insufficient slope; increase sensitivity to recent returns (steepen the first ~15–20 days).",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: underprediction is largest in the mid-horizon (about days 7–25), where realized prices keep grinding higher while forecasts flatten; add a positive drift term that accumulates over this window.",
    "Post-spike behavior: after a sharp upward move, the model mean-reverts too quickly (predicts pullbacks/flat) while outcomes often continue higher; damp mean-reversion strength following upside breakouts.",
    "Volatility compression: forecast amplitude is too low (misses highs); widen forecast distribution / allow higher peaks when recent realized volatility increases."
  ]
}
